{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked your account and it's active with no sign-in problems, and your mailbox is at about 30% of its quota, so storage isn't the cause. Could you please try these steps and let us know the result? First, make sure your computer is turned on and connected to the network, then fully close and reopen Outlook. If orders@ still doesn't appear, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) and check whether orders@ is listed there, using Add shared folder or mailbox if needed. Please also tell us whether you can see orders@ on the web and whether you could send from it before. Once we have that, we can work out the next step.",
  "internal_note": "Checked per KB-011. Account active, not locked, sign-in not blocked, 0 failed logins, must_change_password false. Mailbox 29.7% used (15.2 GB of 50 GB), so not a quota issue (KB-010 not applicable). Desktop BL-DT-0108 shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:09 UTC, no disk warnings (78% free). Possibly just powered off outside the user's 06:00-14:00 Chicago hours; not confirmed. I have no tool to view shared mailbox delegation, so I could not confirm whether the orders@ Full Access or Send As permission still exists. Next steps for the user: restart Outlook and check Outlook on the web. If the web view also lacks orders@ or the user was never granted access, escalate per KB-011/KB-006 (owner approval, then Tier 2 change). If it shows on the web, add it manually per KB-011 fix step 2. Ask whether the device is online at the user's start of shift. Reopened ticket for the user's reply.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
